ebrew/Yiddish Igrot Kodesh Volume 2"},{"key":"url:https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/article_cdo/aid/4666350/jewish/page.htm","id":"chabad-letter-4666350","title":"Igrot Kodesh volume 2 item 4666350","summary":"","source_class":"Igrot Kodesh","status":"Verified","canonical_status":"Verified","context_status":"partial","context_status_raw":null,"date":null,"language":"Hebrew/Yiddish","source_url":"https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/article_cdo/aid/4666350/jewish/page.htm","aid":null,"locator":null,"rights_status":"copyrighted-link-only","publisher_terms":["Igrot Kodesh","Volume 2"],"research_terms":[],"relations":[],"canonical_file":"data/items/igrot-kodesh-vol2-4666350.json","documented_circumstances":null,"question_or_problem":null,"response_propositions":[],"conditions_or_qualifications":[],"audience":null,"verification_scope":"publisher edition","witness_provenance":"authorized Kehot/Chabad.org item-level publisher page","evidence_family_id":null,"primary_secondary_status":null,"has_content_evidence":false,"proposition_origin":null,"proposition_verbatim":null,"evidence_integrity_issues":[],"search_text":"Igrot Kodesh volume 2 item 4666350  Igrot Kodesh Hebrew/Yiddish Igrot Kodesh Volume 2"},{"key":"url:https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/821811/jewish/Obstacles-and-Challenges.htm","id":"chabad-original-draft-aid-821811","title":"Obstacles and Challenges","summary":"","source_class":"Chabad.org correspondence draft","status":"Verified","canonical_status":"Verified","context_status":"complete","context_status_raw":null,"date":null,"language":"English","source_url":"https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/821811/jewish/Obstacles-and-Challenges.htm","aid":null,"locator":null,"rights_status":"bounded Hebrew research paraphrases and locator only","publisher_terms":[],"research_terms":[],"relations":[],"canonical_file":"data/items/mixed-authorized-content-2026-11-12-039.json","documented_circumstances":"טיוטת מענה לאדם שנפגע מהפסד בעסק שמימן פעילות Lubavitch House.","question_or_problem":null,"response_propositions":["הטיוטה מכירה במצוקת הנמען לאחר הפסד בעסק שהכנסותיו יועדו לפעילות ציבורית, אך מבקשת לפרש את המקרה גם במסגרת מבט תורני.","סיפורי התורה מוצגים כבעלי מסר מעשי החורג מזמנם ומקומם, ולכן ניסיון אברהם משמש כאן מסגרת להתמודדות עם קושי כלכלי.","ההדרכה אינה להפסיק את העבודה הציבורית אלא להשתחרר ממחשבות מטרידות ולהמשיך בפעילות תורה וחינוך מתוך שמחה."],"conditions_or_qualifications":["המו״ל מבהיר שהנוסח הסופי אינו בידו ואולי שונה.","הפסד העסק, ההקדשה וההתפתחויות המאוחרות לא אומתו ממסמכים חיצוניים."],"audience":null,"verification_scope":"Complete visible publisher draft inspected; final letter, business records and outcomes not inspected.","witness_provenance":"Chabad.org published original secretarial draft, aid 821811","evidence_family_id":"original-draft-aid-821811-business-loss","primary_secondary_status":"authorized-publisher-secretarial-draft-not-final-letter","has_content_evidence":true,"proposition_origin":"source_grounded_paraphrase","proposition_verbatim":false,"evidence_integrity_issues":[],"proposition_verification":"source_text_inspected","proposition_source_locator":"Chabad.org aid 821811, draft body from business-loss opening through Pesach closing","search_text":"Obstacles and Challenges  Chabad.org correspondence draft English הטיוטה מכירה במצוקת הנמען לאחר הפסד בעסק שהכנסותיו יועדו לפעילות ציבורית, אך מבקשת לפרש את המקרה גם במסגרת מבט תורני. סיפורי התורה מוצגים כבעלי מסר מעשי החורג מזמנם ומקומם, ולכן ניסיון אברהם משמש כאן מסגרת להתמודדות עם קושי כלכלי. ההדרכה אינה להפסיק את העבודה הציבורית אלא להשתחרר ממחשבות מטרידות ולהמשיך בפעילות תורה וחינוך מתוך שמחה. המו״ל מבהיר שהנוסח הסופי אינו בידו ואולי שונה. הפסד העסק, ההקדשה וההתפתחויות המאוחרות לא אומתו ממסמכים חיצוניים."},{"key":"url:https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/887542/jewish/The-Childless-Womans-Role-in-Judaism.htm","id":"chabad-letter-887542","title":"The Childless Woman’s Role in Judaism","summary":"","source_class":"Written responses - authorized publisher English presentation","status":"Verified","canonical_status":"Verified","context_status":"unknown","context_status_raw":"linked-context; page records that Donna L. Halper had written regarding the role of childless women","date":null,"language":"unknown","source_url":"https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/887542/jewish/The-Childless-Womans-Role-in-Judaism.htm","aid":null,"locator":"Chabad.org aid 887542","rights_status":"copyrighted-source; bounded research paraphrases and link only; no protected full text copied","publisher_terms":[],"research_terms":[],"relations":[],"canonical_file":"data/items/chabad-letter-887542.json","documented_circumstances":"Reply dated 13 Iyar 5737 to Donna L. Halper after she asked about the place of a woman unable to bear children; only the publisher's description of the incoming question is available here.","question_or_problem":null,"response_propositions":["The response rejects a hierarchy of value between women and men, describing their distinct functions as mutually necessary rather than superior and inferior.","When circumstances beyond a person's control prevent a mitzvah, the letter applies the principle that incapacity is excused and sincere intent is credited.","It encourages questions that can be understood while maintaining that practice should not be suspended until every reason is intellectually resolved."],"conditions_or_qualifications":[],"audience":null,"verification_scope":"The authorized publisher's English item text and its same-page recipient context note were inspected. The propositions are bounded non-verbatim research paraphrases; the incoming letter, physical original and original-language witness were not inspected.","witness_provenance":"Chabad.org authorized item-level English presentation, AID 887542","evidence_family_id":"original-letter-aid-887542","primary_secondary_status":"authorized publisher English translation/presentation; derived, non-independent witness","has_content_evidence":true,"proposition_origin":"source_grounded_paraphrase","proposition_verbatim":false,"evidence_integrity_issues":[],"proposition_verification":"source_text_inspected","proposition_source_locator":"publisher page, lines 265-290: recipient context, equal value/distinct roles, incapacity, and questioning","search_text":"The Childless Woman’s Role in Judaism  Written responses - authorized publisher English presentation unknown The response rejects a hierarchy of value between women and men, describing their distinct functions as mutually necessary rather than superior and inferior. When circumstances beyond a person's control prevent a mitzvah, the letter applies the principle that incapacity is excused and sincere intent is credited. It encourages questions that can be understood while maintaining that practice should not be suspended until every reason is intellectually resolved. Chabad.org aid 887542"},{"key":"url:https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/1874447/jewish/Woman-of-Valor.htm","id":"chabad-letter-1874447","title":"Woman of Valor","summary":"","source_class":"Written responses - authorized publisher English presentation","status":"Verified","canonical_status":"Verified","context_status":"unknown","context_status_raw":"full-page context available; addressed to editors of A Woman of Valor anthology","date":null,"language":"unknown","source_url":"https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/1874447/jewish/Woman-of-Valor.htm","aid":null,"locator":"Chabad.org aid 1874447","rights_status":"copyrighted-source; bounded research paraphrases and link only; no protected full text copied","publisher_terms":[],"research_terms":[],"relations":[],"canonical_file":"data/items/chabad-letter-1874447.json","documented_circumstances":"Letter dated 18 Elul 5735 to the editors of the planned anthology A Woman of Valor, answering their request for remarks on the role of Jewish women.","question_or_problem":null,"response_propositions":["The letter presents the Jewish home as shaped in daily details, not only on sacred days, by Torah practice and awareness of the Divine.","It assigns the wife and mother a central role in the home's religious atmosphere, including kashrut, Shabbat candle-lighting and family purity.","It calls for broad educational activity by Jewish women and welcomes further responsible publication on these subjects."],"conditions_or_qualifications":[],"audience":null,"verification_scope":"The authorized publisher's English item text was inspected. The propositions are bounded non-verbatim research paraphrases; the physical original, original-language text and editorial translation history were not inspected.","witness_provenance":"Chabad.org authorized item-level English presentation, AID 1874447","evidence_family_id":"original-letter-aid-1874447","primary_secondary_status":"authorized publisher English translation/presentation; derived, non-independent witness","has_content_evidence":true,"proposition_origin":"source_grounded_paraphrase","proposition_verbatim":false,"evidence_integrity_issues":[],"proposition_verification":"source_text_inspected","proposition_source_locator":"publisher page, lines 274-294: Jewish-home framework, the Akeres Habayis role, and the closing call for activity","search_text":"Woman of Valor  Written responses - authorized publisher English presentation unknown The letter presents the Jewish home as shaped in daily details, not only on sacred days, by Torah practice and awareness of the Divine. It assigns the wife and mother a central role in the home's religious atmosphere, including kashrut, Shabbat candle-lighting and family purity. It calls for broad educational activity by Jewish women and welcomes further responsible publication on these subjects. Chabad.org aid 1874447"},{"key":"aid:4666220","id":null,"title":"aid:4666220","summary":"","source_class":null,"status":"Verified","canonical_status":"Verified","context_st