 מענה בעניין מצב רפואי וביטחון בה׳","summary":"The published page identifies this as Letter No. 872, dated 23 Teves 5711, to an unnamed recipient. The letter explicitly says it responds to a letter from Thursday of Parshas Vayechi reporting several operations. The incoming letter itself is not reproduced. Letter No. 937 later contains an editorial cross-reference to Letter No. 872 and its cited sources in connection with the Chabad maxim 'Tracht gut, vet zain gut'.","source_class":"Igrot Kodesh","status":"Linked","canonical_status":"Linked","context_status":"partial","context_status_raw":null,"date":"5711-10-23","language":"English translation of Hebrew/Yiddish correspondence","source_url":"https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/2243668/jewish/Advice-concerning-the-response-to-a-medical-issue-the-importance-of-bitachon-trust-in-G-d.htm","aid":null,"locator":null,"rights_status":"copyrighted-source; bounded research paraphrases and link only; no protected full text copied","publisher_terms":["medical issue","bitachon","health"],"research_terms":["health guidance","trust in G-d","response to reported medical treatment","attention management","practical directives"],"relations":[{"type":"editorial_cross_reference","target_id":"igrot-kodesh-letter-937","basis":"Footnote 2 of published Letter No. 937 explicitly directs the reader to Letter No. 872 and the sources cited there in connection with 'Tracht gut, vet zain gut'."}],"canonical_file":"data/items/igrot-kodesh-letter-872.json","documented_circumstances":"Letter No. 872, dated 23 Teves 5711, to an unnamed recipient who reported having undergone several operations; the incoming wording and diagnosis are absent.","question_or_problem":null,"response_propositions":["The medical guidance combines following physicians' instructions with avoiding self-directed immersion in medical literature that increases fear and despair.","The recipient is advised to redirect attention from repeated health analysis toward trust in G-d and regular, expanded study of Chassidus.","The response links personal strengthening with communal action through classes, gatherings and financing a substantial chassidic publication."],"conditions_or_qualifications":[],"audience":null,"verification_scope":"The authorized publisher's English translation was inspected. Propositions are bounded paraphrases of the outgoing response; the diagnosis, incoming letter, physical original and original-language witness were not inspected. This is historical-source description, not medical advice.","witness_provenance":"Sichos in English English translation published on Chabad.org; underlying original manuscript not inspected","evidence_family_id":"original-letter-aid-2243668","primary_secondary_status":"authorized publisher English translation by Eli Touger; derived, non-independent witness","has_content_evidence":true,"proposition_origin":"source_grounded_paraphrase","proposition_verbatim":false,"evidence_integrity_issues":[],"proposition_verification":"source_text_inspected","proposition_source_locator":"publisher translation, lines 278-285: medical response, attention guidance, trust, study and communal action","search_text":"אגרת מס׳ 872 — מענה בעניין מצב רפואי וביטחון בה׳ The published page identifies this as Letter No. 872, dated 23 Teves 5711, to an unnamed recipient. The letter explicitly says it responds to a letter from Thursday of Parshas Vayechi reporting several operations. The incoming letter itself is not reproduced. Letter No. 937 later contains an editorial cross-reference to Letter No. 872 and its cited sources in connection with the Chabad maxim 'Tracht gut, vet zain gut'. Igrot Kodesh 5711-10-23 English translation of Hebrew/Yiddish correspondence medical issue bitachon health health guidance trust in G-d response to reported medical treatment attention management practical directives The medical guidance combines following physicians' instructions with avoiding self-directed immersion in medical literature that increases fear and despair. The recipient is advised to redirect attention from repeated health analysis toward trust in G-d and regular, expanded study of Chassidus. The response links personal strengthening with communal action through classes, gatherings and financing a substantial chassidic publication."},{"key":"url:https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/2244167/jewish/An-allusion-in-the-letters-associated-with-the-Hebrew-year-5711.htm","id":"igrot-kodesh-letter-926","title":"Letter No. 926 — reply concerning a scheduled meeting and an allusion to the year 5711","summary":"The public item page identifies the recipient as R. Efraim Eliezer HaKohen Yolles and states that the letter responds to his report that a meeting had been scheduled concerning his affairs. The incoming letter is not present. The response asks to be informed of good news and develops a Torah allusion associated with the year 5711.","source_class":"Igrot Kodesh","status":"Indexed","canonical_status":"Indexed","context_status":"partial","context_status_raw":null,"date":"5711-22-Adar-I","language":"English translation of original correspondence","source_url":"https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/2244167/jewish/An-allusion-in-the-letters-associated-with-the-Hebrew-year-5711.htm","aid":null,"locator":null,"rights_status":"copyrighted-source; bounded research paraphrases and link only; no protected full text copied","publisher_terms":["5711","correspondence"],"research_terms":["response to incoming report","request for follow-up news","Torah allusion"],"relations":[],"canonical_file":"data/items/igrot-kodesh-letter-926.json","documented_circumstances":"Letter No. 926 to R. Efraim Eliezer HaKohen Yolles, dated 22 Adar I 5711, responding to news of a scheduled meeting concerning his affairs.","question_or_problem":null,"response_propositions":["The writer asks to be informed of favorable results from a scheduled meeting so that he may share 